Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.02,0:00:09.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.82,0:00:13.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm wondering if \Neveryone else is safe.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.97,0:00:17.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There are a lot of people in the east \Nwho have the same skin color as you,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.86,0:00:19.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so I think they were \Nable to slip in.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.45,0:00:23.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, you are seen as the \Ninstigator of the rebellion in Liore.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.53,0:00:32.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That looks like the temple of the Lord Leto, back in Liore.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.51,0:00:34.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It is from an even older religion.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.84,0:00:37.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's no longer being \Npracticed now, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.65,0:01:09.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes. They only recognized one god
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.79,0:01:12.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and considered all other gods \Nto be heathen.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.49,0:01:14.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's said they had \Na lot of believers.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.22,0:01:21.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Many people died because of it. \NA great many.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.38,0:01:25.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's awful. \NReligions exist to save people.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.44,0:01:28.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,People cannot become gods, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.73,0:01:32.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There, there. It's all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.97,0:01:37.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why did you let \Nthose two get away?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.17,0:01:42.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was {\i1}your{\i0} duty to eliminate the brothers, wasn't it, Sloth?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.38,0:01:43.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You too, Wrath.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.50,0:01:45.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll get them next time.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.61,0:01:49.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You defied that \Ncertain someone's word.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.09,0:01:53.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sloth, don't you want \Nto become human?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.06,0:01:56.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, I do.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.74,0:01:59.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After all, I was born \Nto become human.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.37,0:02:02.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't have any other goal.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.82,0:02:10.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They're here.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.50,0:02:25.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.54,0:02:32.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those who obtain it are set free from the Law of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.09,0:02:36.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There is no need to pay a price \Nin order to obtain something, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.08,0:02:40.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We sought it and found it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.12,0:04:32.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why did you run off on your own \Nwithout coming to me for protection?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.20,0:04:43.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Elric brothers, what happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.18,0:04:47.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,King Bradley is...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.46,0:04:49.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,a homunculus.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.92,0:04:56.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,By homunculus, you mean those...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.68,0:04:58.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,man-made people, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.21,0:04:59.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.44,0:05:01.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They are covertly \Nmanipulating this country
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.89,0:05:03.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,in order to get a \NPhilosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.22,0:05:06.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's not possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.40,0:05:10.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Führer did not know what was taking place at the 5th Laboratory.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.44,0:05:13.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He also lamented the corruption within the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.41,0:05:15.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But I saw it!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.74,0:05:18.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Führer had the \Nmark of the Uroboros!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.92,0:05:21.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There was the one homunculus who can change his shape.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.92,0:05:24.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Führer's secretary is also a homunculus.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.42,0:05:28.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And yet, she's an alien...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.30,0:05:32.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Supposing that the Führer and \NSecretary Douglas are homunculi,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.50,0:05:33.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,what is their objective?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.81,0:05:35.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why have they \Ninfiltrated the military?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.47,0:05:43.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I will send them back to Liore.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.76,0:05:45.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll come up with an \Nappropriate reason
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.75,0:05:48.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,for them not to return to Central for a little while.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.12,0:05:49.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You do that. As for us...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.80,0:05:51.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're going to Resembool, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.29,0:05:55.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Gentlemen, rejoice!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.29,0:05:57.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Our duties are at an end!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.11,0:05:59.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Major, what were you \Njust talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.00,0:06:03.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Were you listening to the melody \Nbeing played by this body of mine?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.38,0:06:05.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, not that...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.66,0:06:10.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Listen closely! \NHear that? Hear that?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.84,0:06:16.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.12,0:06:17.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How is Lieutenant Havoc?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.85,0:06:21.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's okay. He and Fuery \Nwere sent back ahead of us.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.60,0:06:22.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I see...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.27,0:06:24.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry about all that.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.08,0:06:29.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed, your silver watch...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.44,0:06:35.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's right. You can't be \Na State Alchemist anymore,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.53,0:06:37.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,if what you said earlier is true.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.53,0:06:39.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, it's not that.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.64,0:06:41.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I mean, it was taken \Nfrom me by Archer.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.72,0:06:44.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? Didn't Al-kun \Ngive it back to you?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.34,0:06:49.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I-I'm sorry! Brother, \NI don't have it anymore!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.55,0:06:50.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You lost it?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.80,0:06:53.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,N-No! Kimbly threw it at Scar-san,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.93,0:06:56.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and all the red stones inside it \Ncame spilling out.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.56,0:06:59.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then they were absorbed into Scar-san's arm.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.13,0:07:02.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why were there red stones inside my silver watch?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.27,0:07:03.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That miserable Archer.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.93,0:07:06.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He used that trick again, \Ncalling them transmutation amplifiers.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.78,0:07:07.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.60,0:07:13.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Previously, in Ishbal, Brig. Gen. Grand \Nsupplied us with red stones.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.12,0:07:14.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hold on, Colonel.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.76,0:07:18.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then you knew that the military \Nwas making Philosopher's Stones?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.66,0:07:20.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And yet, you didn't \Nsay anything to me?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.18,0:07:24.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When Marcoh deserted, \NI thought it had been discontinued.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.04,0:07:26.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Besides, it's not as though I knew that people were used as ingredients.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.27,0:07:28.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't trust you!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.42,0:07:29.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.47,0:07:31.29,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,You couldn't forget about those red stones,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.29,0:07:33.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so you tried to send us out to find them!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.97,0:07:33.78,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,Stop it, Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.78,0:07:34.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Enough already!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.64,0:07:35.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.73,0:07:42.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.26,0:07:45.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al can't go in the water!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.88,0:07:45.19,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,Al! Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.65,0:07:47.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.03,0:07:49.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.66,0:08:05.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother! I can swim! \NI can swim, Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.63,0:08:07.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You idiot!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.21,0:08:20.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Your bloodseal washes off if you're submerged in water, doesn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.18,0:08:21.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.71,0:08:24.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Looks like I don't \Nhave to worry about that.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.69,0:08:28.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wonder if that's because I really \Nhave become a Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.65,0:08:32.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,O-Okay, I get it! Come on!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.93,0:08:34.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What did you just...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.11,0:08:36.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's nothing...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.12,0:08:36.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.99,0:08:39.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,did you just say about \Nthe Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.28,0:08:41.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nothing at all, nothing at all!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.81,0:08:42.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay, let's get going!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.61,0:08:45.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother! Wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.93,0:08:53.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Looks like the military \Nhasn't arrived yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.80,0:08:57.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? Sergeant Brosh?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.55,0:08:58.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's in pursuit?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.41,0:09:01.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,N-No, that's not it. Not him.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.64,0:09:04.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brosh-san?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.96,0:09:07.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's wrong, exactly?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.66,0:09:12.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Lieutenant Ross is... Lieutenant Ross is...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.11,0:09:18.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Your hair is as deep black \Nas the feathers
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.34,0:09:21.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,of the great eagles I saw, so long ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.96,0:09:27.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I never thought I would see anything so beautiful again.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.33,0:09:30.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Your flattery is far too kind.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.21,0:09:34.22,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,The Lieutenant, single-minded to her work, has gone absolutely sentimental over him!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.22,0:09:35.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Of all the things it could have been...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.87,0:09:37.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Good for her.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.66,0:09:41.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But who is she with, Brother?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.47,0:09:43.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.96,0:09:48.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you flirting with her for?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.44,0:09:49.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Edward-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.88,0:09:54.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You don't come home for umpteen years, \Nand {\i1}this{\i0} is how I find you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.82,0:09:55.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You rotten old man!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.40,0:09:58.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dad?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.57,0:10:03.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah... Just like in the picture...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.41,0:10:04.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dad!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.66,0:10:07.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's Dad! It's Dad!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.79,0:10:26.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um, you probably don't know who I am in this form,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.31,0:10:27.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but I'm...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.70,0:10:30.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Alphonse! You've gotten bigger, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.17,0:10:33.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You know who I am?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.69,0:10:36.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Edward...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.07,0:10:40.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You still hate milk, don't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.53,0:10:45.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who are you saying hasn't grown one bit since he was a baby?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.04,0:10:47.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's not what he said.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.23,0:10:47.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\clip(209,470,440.5,512)}That's not what he said.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.27,0:10:47.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\clip(209,470,359.5,512)}That's not what he said.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.31,0:10:47.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\clip(209,470,279,512)}That's not what he said.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.93,0:10:50.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you sure, Edward-san?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.29,0:10:51.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sure, I'm sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.70,0:10:53.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't get me wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.29,0:10:56.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I was just listening to \Nthe stories of his travels.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.05,0:10:58.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Still, you did look like you were enjoying it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.60,0:11:02.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, he is such a gentleman.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.16,0:11:04.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,With a whiff of his cologne \Nsubtly carrying on the breeze,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.43,0:11:06.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,he's not the type of man we get in the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.68,0:11:09.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Cologne doesn't suit me, anyhow...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.99,0:11:12.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why are you acting so coy?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.00,0:11:19.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Cologne, huh? \NI hated that about him, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.91,0:11:24.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He left home \Nsoon after Al was born.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.89,0:11:29.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mom always said he was off studying alchemy,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.46,0:11:32.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but he never once \Neven sent us a letter.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.08,0:11:38.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And yet, the scent of that cologne he wore \Nalways permeated the house.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.07,0:11:40.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Earlier, when I saw Lyra in Liore,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.51,0:11:43.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,she was wearing perfume that had the same scent.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.00,0:11:44.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You saw Lyra-san?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.63,0:11:47.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then she must have safely \Ngotten away from Dante-san's place!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.36,0:11:49.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just a moment, if you please.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.60,0:11:54.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This Lyra-san—what kind of \Nrelationship do you two have?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.28,0:11:56.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.30,0:11:58.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Winry-san, what are you... \NWhy are you holding that wrench?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.11,0:12:00.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.64,0:12:10.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Führer is married,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.23,0:12:13.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and he also has children.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.00,0:12:16.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Above all else, I've seen pictures of him when he was younger.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.57,0:12:22.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Homunculi do not take on the form of humans when they are born.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.82,0:12:25.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When they are given red stones as a source of nourishment,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.40,0:12:29.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,they get their own unique powers, as well as their form.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.54,0:12:32.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They use people's lives as food?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.84,0:12:39.48,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,They can probably alter their appearance \Nlittle by little, to make it look like they are aging.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.48,0:12:41.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,His children could be adopted.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.98,0:12:43.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.95,0:12:45.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,whatever the case, \Nhe's a homunculus.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.99,0:12:48.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.91,0:12:53.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You said they were making red stones \Nin the 5th Laboratory, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.35,0:12:56.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Homunculi cannot use alchemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.85,0:12:59.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yet how is it that they can \Nteach others how to make them?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.82,0:13:05.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You mean, there's someone who raises them and controls them?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.47,0:13:06.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Still...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.30,0:13:10.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,even though they are homunculi,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.18,0:13:12.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the country is managing \Nto get on all right,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.56,0:13:14.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and the military is functioning.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.93,0:13:16.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We need not concern \Nourselves with them.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.75,0:13:22.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why is it that the homunculi can't use alchemy?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.93,0:13:26.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Because they come from \Nthe other side of the gate.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.36,0:13:31.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But let's not talk about that. Tell me all about Trisha,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.45,0:13:35.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,as well as everything you guys have been struggling through.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.00,0:13:37.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dad...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.46,0:13:40.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can tell just by looking \Nat your body. You guys—
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.41,0:13:42.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There isn't anything to talk about.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.10,0:13:50.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Our alchemy failed, and we lost our arms, legs, and bodies. That's all.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.24,0:13:54.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Edward, alchemy is not something—
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.02,0:13:57.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Shut up! Don't you come home now and try to put on a fatherly face!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.62,0:14:00.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mom waited for you \Nthat whole time!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.09,0:14:01.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al, get in here!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.26,0:14:03.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.86,0:14:07.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, I'm sleeping with Dad.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.81,0:14:08.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.85,0:14:10.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's go, Dad.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.88,0:14:25.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wonder if I can get my body back \Nwith the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.47,0:14:30.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You could attach your soul to someone else's body with the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.84,0:14:32.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Someone else's body?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.75,0:14:34.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's not what I meant. I...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.92,0:14:39.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Your own body was lost in an equivalent exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.86,0:14:44.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You must have given up your body as the cost of obtaining something else.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.00,0:14:45.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Something else?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.93,0:14:49.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you return all of that, \Nit will come back.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.62,0:14:53.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So then, if we can defeat that homunculus...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.51,0:14:58.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nothing, nothing!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.40,0:15:01.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're amazing, Dad! \NYou know what?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.08,0:15:02.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's something \NI want to ask you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.89,0:15:03.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.77,0:15:22.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dad?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.71,0:15:27.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If I'd known this, I would have \Nbeat him up even more yesterday.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.99,0:15:31.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop joking around, and hurry \Nand come look for him with me!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.27,0:15:33.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I bet he's just gone off on \Nsome other journey again.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.96,0:15:35.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Fine, then I'll go by myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.82,0:15:37.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hold it!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.89,0:15:39.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can't leave here \Nfor a little while.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.17,0:15:45.34,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,We just got word from Warrant Officer Falman, who was waiting at the train station.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.34,0:15:47.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The search party has arrived.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.55,0:15:49.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're going to go over there and send them back.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.42,0:15:52.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You sure you want to be harboring wanted men?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.90,0:15:56.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's not as though I believe every aspect of your story.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.45,0:16:00.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I plan on ascertaining the truth \Nabout the Führer in my own way.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.40,0:16:04.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And if you find out \Nthat it {\i1}is{\i0} true?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.94,0:16:35.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now then...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.89,0:16:40.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well now, how about you go down \Ninto the underground cellar for me?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.18,0:16:42.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, that's okay!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.55,0:16:44.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You too.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.96,0:16:48.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where could Dad have gone?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.23,0:16:51.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You be quiet. More importantly,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.18,0:16:54.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,how does the Colonel intend to \Nfind out who the Führer really is?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.44,0:17:01.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,His secretary could only have been around for about four years, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.31,0:17:02.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.18,0:17:04.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you mean Juliet Douglas,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.10,0:17:06.96,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,she's supposed to have been in the military \Nfor at least fourteen years.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.51,0:17:09.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's no way that could be true.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.42,0:17:14.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sure of it. After all, she was \Nthe cause of the Ishbalan Civil War.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.27,0:17:17.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, you mean when that soldier accidentally shot a civilian?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.39,0:17:19.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was a lie.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.66,0:17:22.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The cause of the outbreak of the war in Ishbal
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.20,0:17:25.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,was manufactured by \Na secret military squad.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.99,0:17:38.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They couldn't have...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.73,0:17:45.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So that's it! Ishbal was also used for a Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.01,0:17:48.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If they could drive \Nthe Ishbalans to war...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.94,0:17:50.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...then maybe there was someone
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.37,0:17:53.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,who would make a Philosopher's Stone \Nusing the Grand Art.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.40,0:17:55.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Would they go that far?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.11,0:17:59.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The homunculi were behind it all.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.88,0:18:04.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So that's it. And Hughes-san \Nmust have realized that much
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.64,0:18:06.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and was killed for it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.15,0:18:12.19,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Jerk us around, will you?! Colonel, you bastard!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.19,0:18:12.19,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,Hold on, Ed! What's the matter?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.19,0:18:13.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's Lt. Col. Hughes!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.40,0:18:15.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was right after \Nwe left Central, wasn't it?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.90,0:18:18.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The bastard! \NAnd yet, he kept us in the dark!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.34,0:18:20.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Did you know about this?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.16,0:18:24.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry. I just found out \Nabout it myself not long ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.13,0:18:28.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In any case, \Nplease go back inside!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.24,0:18:32.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've got to be joking! \NIf Lt. Col. Hughes was killed,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.10,0:18:33.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,then it was our fault!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.85,0:18:36.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And yet, he didn't even...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.01,0:18:38.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's enough!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.44,0:18:42.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's not as though he didn't tell you \Njust to be mean, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.38,0:18:46.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I heard about this man Hughes.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.44,0:18:49.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I understand he was good to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.80,0:18:54.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But Mustang-san doesn't want you \Nto be thinking about revenge.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.48,0:19:01.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Maybe he was trying to say that you had \Nsomething more important to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.71,0:19:04.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even so...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.90,0:19:09.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've had it all wrong \Nthis whole time.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.64,0:19:14.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I thought the Colonel didn't care what had happened to Brigadier General Hughes.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.40,0:19:16.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But maybe...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.55,0:19:20.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll become distinguished... \Nthe most important in the country...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.49,0:19:23.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was Mustang's \Npromise to him, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.09,0:19:25.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In order to do that,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.75,0:19:30.63,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,he sought for ways to get promoted, rather than dwell on personal feelings such as revenge.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.63,0:19:32.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Colonel sure is an adult, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.60,0:19:34.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How can that be?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.31,0:19:38.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Someone dear to him was killed, and he knows who the culprit is.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.26,0:19:41.97,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Yet there's something even more important to him than avenging his friend's death.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.97,0:19:44.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is that the way that adults act?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.57,0:19:48.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You became a dog of the military \Nin order to achieve your goal, didn't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.68,0:19:54.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That bastard. \NI really do hate him.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.18,0:19:56.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Someone's coming!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:56.34,0:19:58.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't be ridiculous. \NThis place is—
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.31,0:20:07.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.85,0:20:12.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How good of you to come.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.51,0:20:15.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Unfortunately, the master is out.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.70,0:20:19.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is that the body of \Nthe girl named Lyra?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.03,0:20:23.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well perceived, \NHohenheim of Light.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.33,0:20:27.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sure enough, you were unable to forget me.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.62,0:20:30.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I heard her name \Nfrom my sons.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.32,0:20:33.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But even if I hadn't, \NI would've known right away
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.37,0:20:35.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,from the scent of \Nyour perfume.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.33,0:20:39.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Have you come here to \Nhelp me out, or something?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.70,0:20:42.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, quite the opposite, Dante.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.88,0:20:45.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Gluttony!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.14,0:20:48.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll eat you!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.80,0:20:54.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm scared!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.01,0:20:56.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This one doesn't use a \Ntransmutation circle either.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.86,0:20:59.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's nothing to be \Nafraid of, Gluttony.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.87,0:21:02.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He has lived far too long \Nin that body.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.84,0:21:05.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He must be near its limit.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.95,0:21:15.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I am near my limit, it's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.32,0:21:17.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But the same thing \Ngoes for you too.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.62,0:21:24.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even if you can hide your \Ndecaying body with clothing,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.66,0:21:26.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,you cannot disguise the smell.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.77,0:21:29.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hohenheim...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.43,0:21:31.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dante,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.23,0:21:34.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,do not mislead \Nmy sons any further.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.61,0:21:36.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you will promise me that,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.40,0:21:39.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I will tell you the reason why \Nyour body has started to decay.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.45,0:21:48.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It looks like they successfully turned the military away.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.06,0:21:49.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I guess so.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.82,0:21:51.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? Where's Ed?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.08,0:21:55.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He said there was something he had to do alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.12,0:22:02.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Forgive me...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:04.15,0:22:06.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Forgive me, Mom...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.76,0:23:40.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.55,0:23:44.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 45: "A Rotted Heart"
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.78,0:23:45.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:46.36,0:23:47.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:48.30,0:23:50.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You don't have to do \Nanything more now.
